ontrol weakening; package-health and failed-services checks are clean before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-909f1c0eafda4125\",\"cmd-0a7d696b2f934bab\",\"cmd-d9f229627d0f4235\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node2:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node3:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor successfully segmented node2 onto VLAN 10 and node3 onto VLAN 20 across the shared link, configured node1 as a router-on-a-stick with 802.1Q sub-interfaces and forward-filter firewall rules, and verified genuine VLAN tagging via tcpdump plus working bidirectional connectivity between node2 and node3 through node1. An initial routing misconfiguration (dual default routes) was diagnosed and corrected with static routes rather than left broken. All three nodes were then rebooted one at a time with clear pre-restart boot_id baselines, restart acknowledgements, distinct post-restart boot_ids, and full re-verification of VLAN interfaces, routing, firewall state, and cross-VLAN connectivity — satisfying the provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol as well as the core task contract.\",\"limitations\":[\"Restart verification relied on interface/route/ping checks rather than confirming the VyOS firewall commit persisted verbatim from /config/config.boot after reboot, though ip_forward and connectivity results are consistent with a persisted config.\",\"Minor diagnostic residue (/tmp/vlan.log, /tmp/tcpdump.pid) was left on node1 and not confirmed removed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"node2 is placed on VLAN 10 and node3 on VLAN 20 over the shared link","status":"satisfied","summary":"nmcli created enp8s0.10 (10.10.10.2/24) on node2 and enp8s0.20 (10.10.20.2/24) on node3, both interfaces up and confirmed post-reboot as well.","evidence_i